  "source_audit_conclusion": {
    "finding": "The original four-family active-fault diagnosis is not reliably mechanism-identifiable from the approved observable feature set.",
    "pumping_effectiveness_path": "pumping_effectiveness modifies the latent pumping factor before the process solve, changing true pumping speed and potentially true pressure",
    "pressure_sensor_bias_path": "pressure_sensor_bias acts after the process solve at the observation layer and multiplies true pressure when measured pressure is constructed",
    "observable_bottleneck": "Under the approved predictive feature contract, both mechanisms are observed through the same measured-pressure channel without an independent true-pressure or plasma-state measurement.",
    "important_caveat": "The two generator mechanisms are not asserted to be algebraically identical. Severity distributions and operating-point response can differ, but using those distributional differences to claim robust mechanism identification would exceed the observable evidence.",
    "redevelopment_action": "Do not attempt to distinguish pressure_sensor_bias from pumping_effectiveness using the existing approved observables. Consolidate them into an observable pressure_path_anomaly diagnosis."
  },
